---
/** Evidence 3 of 3: the page robots.txt asks crawlers to skip. Not in the sitemap. */
import { flags } from '../../data/ctf';
const flag = flags[2].flag;
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Evidence locker</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/evidence-locker/locker.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <span class="tag">EVIDENCE 3 OF 3</span>
      <h1>You walked straight past the robots.txt sign.</h1>
      <p>A <code class="inline-code">Disallow</code> line is a polite request to crawlers, not access control. Anything it lists is still one request away.</p>
      <code>{flag}</code>
      <p>Submit it on the main page: press <strong>Ctrl K</strong> (or <strong>/</strong>) and type <strong>submit</strong> followed by the flag.</p>
      <p><a href="/">Back to the case file</a></p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
